\GitHub\\TrendVault-Program\\StoryVault-Video-Factory\\data\\narration\\vid_mq8eq0hmc5d7647d0a_final.wav","overlay_ass_path":"C:\\Users\\Anton\\OneDrive\\Documents\\GitHub\\TrendVault-Program\\StoryVault-Video-Factory\\data\\captions\\vid_mq8eq0hmc5d7647d0a_overlay.ass","total_duration":55.978,"intro_meta":"{\"topicEnd\":5.331,\"introEnd\":7.639,\"total\":55.978}","voice_preset_id":null,"preview_url":"/media/previews/vid_mq8eq0hmc5d7647d0a.mp4"},"story":{"id":"story_mq8c8ez58956ea5e29","title":"AITA for publicly calling out my wife's friend over her surprise wedding fees?","url":null,"community":"r/AmItheAsshole","source_type":"file","warnings":["Strong language"]},"script":{"id":"script_mq8cdemhdc13cb13db","full_text":"My wife is upset with me too. Money has always been tight, so when my wife got invited to her college roommate Dana's destination wedding in Cancun, we agreed that only she would go. My wife was stunned, because the original invitation said nothing about any fees. When my wife politely asked whether the fee could be waived since money was tight, Dana laughed and said that if she couldn't afford to celebrate her, then maybe she wasn't really her friend. She sent a kind message explaining that she could not afford the additional fee, but that she loved Dana and hoped to celebrate with her when she got home. Part of me thinks I defended my family against someone who tried to bankrupt us and then shame us for it. So that is the situation. Am I the asshole here? So tell me — am I the asshole here?","hook":"My wife is upset with me too.","audience_question":"So tell me — am I the asshole here?","word_count":150},"narration":{"id":"narr_mq8cdeml5fec2fce28","voice":"Microsoft Zira Desktop","duration":48.339,"path":"C:\\Users\\Anton\\OneDrive\\Documents\\GitHub\\TrendVault-Program\\StoryVault-Video-Factory\\data\\narration\\narr_mq8cdeml5fec2fce28.wav","file_url":"/media/narration/narr_mq8cdeml5fec2fce28.wav"},"caption":{"id":"cap_mq8eq0h94b17d76104","style":